                <pb facs="0469" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg367"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>No official record of this conversation has been found. The only reference to the
                    meeting occurs in the notes by John P.
                        Davies on what Hopkins
                    told Stilwell and Davies on December 6. According to the
                        Davies notes, Hopkins said that he had had a three-hour
                    conversation with the Chiangs on the evening before his departure for Tehran.
                    With respect to subjects discussed, Hopkins mentioned only that the Chiangs had raised the question
                    of the return of Outer Mongolia. This question had been brought up at the dinner
                    meeting on November 23, 1943; see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg325">p. 325</ref>.</p>
                <p>The Hopkins notes reproduced on the facing
                    page may pertain to this conversation.</p>
            </div>
